{"seq":8,"trial_id":"gbrain-verbs-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-verbs-told-mu-heldout/sc-05-hartford-postmortem/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-25T09:39:04.053Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"f6d5fe8ba4e702337e34c77c2534ebe7ceba52f6ec493ba2d067a9aa72b3ebfa","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1MTZS8410N","text":"Gideon, you first reported the kiosks offline at **10:42 AM on 3 Aug** in #inc-vtg-hartford. The channel history I found has your message as the first entry, so that's the earliest report there. I didn't cover other channels or DMs.\n\nBetween your report and the recovery, the channel records:\n\n- **10:42**: You reported both inbound lanes at Hartford showing a white screen after badge scan, with the guard writing trailer numbers on a clipboard.\n- **10:44**: Mateo reported six trucks waiting at the east gate and his status-page login getting \"access denied.\"\n- **10:45**: Ruth asked for the escalation to stay in this channel.\n- **10:47**: You said Vantorre's scheduling still worked from the dispatch office, and that you had emailed the incident text to procurement.\n- **10:51**: Odile said Carrowmere Cloud was checking the Hartford gateway route and asked that kiosk 2 stay powered on.\n- **10:55**: You noted Mateo's admin account could open Pemberline Dock, so the status-page access problem was separate.\n- **11:03**: Mateo said kiosk 1 was back and the guard had checked in trailer 8836, which dispatch could see.\n- **11:08**: You recorded both lanes working as of 11:07, left the channel open for another arrival cycle, and logged the status-page access issue under INC-4821.\n\nThe channel doesn't say what the guard did after the clipboard, beyond the trailer check-in at 11:03. If the postmortem needs more detail on that, Mateo or the guard's shift log would be the next place to look."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1MTZS8410N","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
